TEST 10 COMPLETE
========================================
For each tilt, verify the pulsing motor is at the
expected position on the frame.

If the wrong motor pulsed:
  1. Note which nn output → which motor index → which pin
  2. Swap the ESC wires so the correct physical motor
     is connected to the correct pin
  3. OR fix NN_TO_MOTOR[] in main.c

========================================
TEST 11: IIR Limit-Cycle Stress Test
========================================
Feeds synthetic NN outputs into the IIR filter.
Detects limit cycles that cause motor pulsing.
No hardware needed — runs immediately (~2 sec).

  Current parameters:
    ALPHA_SLOW  = +0.080
    ALPHA_FAST  = +0.600
    SNAP_THRESH = +0.150

Scenario A: small noise  (0.05↔0.15, amp=0.05, center=0.10)
  Expected: <10 PWM swings, ALPHA_SLOW throughout

  [0] nn=+0.150 iir=+0.090 pwm=1359 a=+0.600
  [100] nn=+0.150 iir=+0.095 pwm=1360 a=+0.080
  [200] nn=+0.150 iir=+0.095 pwm=1360 a=+0.080
  [300] nn=+0.150 iir=+0.095 pwm=1360 a=+0.080
  [400] nn=+0.150 iir=+0.095 pwm=1360 a=+0.080

  Toggles>5us: 0   FAST-alpha ticks: 1
  [PASS] Scenario A: stable — small noise absorbed by ALPHA_SLOW

Scenario B: on-threshold noise  (0.07↔0.23, amp=0.08, center=0.15)
  This is the vibration scenario in flight.
  Expected: FAIL if SNAP_THRESH too close to noise floor

  [0] nn=+0.230 iir=+0.138 pwm=1378 a=+0.600
  [100] nn=+0.230 iir=+0.141 pwm=1379 a=+0.080
  [200] nn=+0.230 iir=+0.141 pwm=1379 a=+0.080
  [300] nn=+0.230 iir=+0.141 pwm=1379 a=+0.080
  [400] nn=+0.230 iir=+0.141 pwm=1379 a=+0.080

  Toggles>5us: 0   FAST-ticks: 1   Alpha-flips: 1
  [PASS] Scenario B: stable — no limit cycle at snap threshold

Scenario C: large step 0.0 → +0.5  (should converge in <15 ticks)

  [0] iir=+0.000 err=-0.500 a=+0.080
  [5] iir=+0.300 err=-0.200 a=+0.600
  [10] iir=+0.443 err=-0.057 a=+0.080
  [20] iir=+0.475 err=-0.025 a=+0.080
  [30] iir=+0.489 err=-0.011 a=+0.080
  [40] iir=+0.495 err=-0.005 a=+0.080
  [50] iir=+0.498 err=-0.002 a=+0.080
  [60] iir=+0.499 err=-0.001 a=+0.080
  [70] iir=+0.500 err=-0.000 a=+0.080
  Converged in 7 ticks after step
  [PASS] Scenario C: FAST path working — large corrections track quickly

---- IIR TUNING GUIDE ----
  If Scenario B FAILED: raise SNAP_THRESH from 0.15 → 0.25.
  If motors still pulse: lower ALPHA_SLOW from 0.08 → 0.05.
  If drone feels sluggish after fix: lower ALPHA_SLOW to 0.10.
  Nuclear option: remove adaptive IIR, use fixed ALPHA = 0.20.

