TEST 12: Loop Timing Jitter & Overrun Detector
========================================
Measures real SysTick period variance and per-phase cost.
Overruns cause AHRS spikes → NN commands → motor pulses.

Board flat. Running 500 ticks (5 sec)...

  [0] period=10000 imu=29 ahrs=3 baro=0 tot=33 us
  [100] period=10000 imu=29 ahrs=3 baro=0 tot=32 us
  [200] period=10000 imu=29 ahrs=3 baro=0 tot=32 us
  [300] period=10000 imu=29 ahrs=3 baro=0 tot=32 us
  [400] period=10000 imu=29 ahrs=3 baro=0 tot=32 us

---- TIMING SUMMARY (500 ticks) ----

  Tick period:   avg=10000 min=10000 max=10000 jitter=0 us
  Overruns (>10500us): 0
  Worst IMU read:   29 us
  Worst AHRS:       3 us
  Worst baro read:  310 us  (fires every 4 ticks — baro I2C blocking cost)
  Worst total tick: 342 us  (budget = 10000 us)
  Budget margin:    9658 us free

---- DIAGNOSTICS ----

  [PASS] No tick overruns — loop body fits within 10 ms period
  [PASS] Tick jitter < 600 us — timing is clean
  [PASS] Baro I2C read < 1500 us — within loop budget

  Note: NN forward pass (~15 us) not included here. Add to tot.

